                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e800d31f-fb5b-46ed-9656-c404547d2acf",
                        "source_entry_id": "eb8666ed-695a-339f-840e-42aed545ea77",
                        "source_sense_id": "c42d8044-e111-3480-bd4e-bcd56c2b5fa6",
                        "target_lang_word": "Kantian",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Kantian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fef7ebb9-b63c-308e-a89c-27196bc52c19",
                                        "entry_id": "3b027bfe-f55d-31b6-bcb6-e0993d9c6a36",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, pertaining to, or resembling the philosophical views of Immanuel Kant (1724-1804)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3564028d-0f9f-4456-a093-bfba2e1e7b92",
                                                "sense_id": "fef7ebb9-b63c-308e-a89c-27196bc52c19",
                                                "text": "Gurwitsch's notion of the perceptual noema as a completely idealized phenomenon is more Kantian than Husserlian."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f866377e-db27-470b-a05a-89f840e128a5",
                                                "sense_id": "fef7ebb9-b63c-308e-a89c-27196bc52c19",
                                                "text": "Thus Django becomes the carrier of the “public use of one's reason”—the Kantian road to enlightenment given to him by the German “Forty-Eighter” dentist–turned-bounty hunter Dr. “King” Schultz, and represents the fictive, allohistorical beginning of the battle against slavery and racism in the United States."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0fba8ada-2c77-49e3-b9a4-65e10c99b97c",
                                                "sense_id": "fef7ebb9-b63c-308e-a89c-27196bc52c19",
                                                "text": "It aimed to pacify intra-European relations through exchange and economic cooperation. The framework was therefore Kantian: it was based on the principle of peace through exchange."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Kantian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6efa7fbf-aa8a-31cb-9c05-865ee40897c4",
                                        "entry_id": "755e27b5-3b66-376b-8782-dc8d8d462a14",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who subscribes to philosophical views associated with Immanuel Kant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "195620f4-14ea-4daf-8ddc-1d2c10ee6a99",
                        "source_entry_id": "eb8666ed-695a-339f-840e-42aed545ea77",
                        "source_sense_id": "c42d8044-e111-3480-bd4e-bcd56c2b5fa6",
                        "target_lang_word": "kantien",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "kantien",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ce7d6a45-2751-3023-b7cd-43e62278da78",
                                        "entry_id": "c243c60b-2595-39da-970b-f141d06ec48d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui découle ou s’apparente à la pensée de Kant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c6fcbc2-4891-4106-b466-15da842746c6",
                                                "sense_id": "ce7d6a45-2751-3023-b7cd-43e62278da78",
                                                "text": "Hier, en France, il fallait être humanitaire, kantien, philosémite. Actuellement, la mode, chez nous, penche vers un christianisme édulcoré."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b06fd91f-4c75-4abc-b12d-c6017c6a6918",
                                                "sense_id": "ce7d6a45-2751-3023-b7cd-43e62278da78",
                                                "text": "Guillaume met en garde la fonctionnaire que je suis contre le respect absolu de la légalité et l'exigence kantienne d'universaliser son action quelles qu'en soient les circonstances."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa5d8a34-f62d-4fc7-a9a8-3a09c23b66a0",
                                                "sense_id": "ce7d6a45-2751-3023-b7cd-43e62278da78",
                                                "text": "– Faut te faire une raison », dit Gabriel dont les propos se nuançaient parfois d’un thomisme légèrement kantien.\nEt, passant sur le plan de la cosubjectivité, il ajouta :\n « Et puis faut se grouiller : Charles attend. »"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "kantien",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3e734f64-d1e3-340e-b5e5-9320437b0615",
                                        "entry_id": "7b15552b-b1dc-30f0-ba12-ddfc0119d721",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Adepte de la pensée de Kant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0456525b-0c0b-4322-b0cf-68d13da03cf6",
                                                "sense_id": "3e734f64-d1e3-340e-b5e5-9320437b0615",
                                                "text": "[…], le philosophe croise des civils allemands qui regardent les captifs comme “une quasi-humanité, une bande de singes”. Seul un chien aboie gaiement devant le cortège : Bobby. Pour lui, écrit Levinas, “nous fûmes des hommes”, des fins en soi ; c’est pourquoi le canidé lui apparaît comme “le dernier kantien de l’Allemagne nazie”."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
